.Dd 2026-10-24
.Dt b64toasc 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm b64toasc
.Nd a tool for decoding a Base64-encoded string to ASCII
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm b64toasc
.Op Fl h
.Ar string
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The command takes Base64-encoded
.Ar string ,
decodes it, and returns an ASCII string.
.Pp
The
.Op -h 
option simply instructs the program to display usage information. No conversion
is done.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The program returns 0 on success, and 1 when an error occurred.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset
b64toasc SGVsbG8sIHdvcmxkIQ==
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr asctob64 1 ,
.Xr b64 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Pp
The program implements Base64 encoding and decoding according to the Internet
Engineering Task Force (IETF) Request For Comments (RFC) 4648 "The Base16,
Base32, and Base64 Data Encodings" standard.
.Pp
.Sh AUTHORS
.Pp
.An John Howie (Howie Consulting Inc.)
.Mt john@howieconsultinginc.com
.Pp
.Sh BUGS
There are no known bugs.
